      "content": "that's getting better, but the score is still coming back way lower than I was hoping for. my manager is going to flag this for being too \"shallow\" if the complexity score isn't up. \n\ncan you expand this out a bit? maybe break down the steps more granularly? like, instead of just one bullet for auth, you could have sub-steps for generating the key, finding it in the portal, and actually using it. and maybe add a few more headers if it helps the score, as long as it doesn't look like total nonsense. just try to get that structural score up a bit more so it passes the automated check.",
